"Robert Marenda" <rmarenda@charter.net> wrote:

>Now for a question or two. When I find a wand, and I do not have a spare 
>scroll of identify, what are some safe ways to identify it? 

Engraving; don't be afraid of losing a charge. If you wish to be spoilt,
read David Damerells object identification spoiler.

>I have also been avoiding using fountains and sinks. I fear drinking from 
>fountains because I keep releasing nasties that kill me. I also have given 
>up on dumping rings down sinks to identify them. Any tips on when to (and 
>when not to) use fountains and sinks? 

Dropping rings into sinks is actually a pretty good way to identify them;
of course, in general they will be lost afterwards. Also, non-cursed
rings can be put on for one move.

I use fountains when I start a wizard with a magic marker to blank my
spellbooks. But many people don't follow this strategy, because of the
inherent risks of dipping. 
